j+(3t-1)\\,k & =2\\,i+4\\,j+8\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+t}=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-5=4 \\\\ 3t-1=8\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get $t=3.$ This value also satifies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,4,8)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(3).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{1+t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1+t}}\\,i+2t\\,j+3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1+(3)}}\\,i+2(3)\\,j+3\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,i+2\\cdot 3\\,j+3\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,i+6\\,j+3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(2,4,8)$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=2i+4\\,j+8\\,k+u(\\frac{1}{4}\\,i+6\\,j+3\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328060 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328061 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328062 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328063 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328064 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1041 "selection" 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328061 13194139535036 true] [17592186328059 1110 #uuid "e6e8dba0-9afc-5189-b1a7-2f8df6214fdb" 13194139535036 true] [17592186328060 1034 "2i+4\\,j+8\\,k+u(\\frac{1}{4}\\,i+3\\,j-3\\,k)" 13194139535036 true] [17592186328060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535036 true] [17592186328060 1111 #uuid "4842bc55-3241-5fdb-bea9-8e8c770f5aae" 13194139535036 true] [17592186328061 1034 "2i+4\\,j+8\\,k+u(\\frac{1}{4}\\